netfilter: nf_tables: use rcu chain hook list iterator from netlink dump path

jira KERNEL-1646
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8
commit-author Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
commit 4ffcf5ca81c3b83180473eb0d3c010a1a7c6c4de
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8/4ffcf5ca.failed

Lockless iteration over hook list is possible from netlink dump path,
use rcu variant to iterate over the hook list as is done with flowtable
hooks.

Fixes: b9703ed44ffb ("netfilter: nf_tables: support for adding new devices to an existing netdev chain")
	Reported-by: Phil Sutter <phil@nwl.cc>
	Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
(cherry picked from commit 4ffcf5ca81c3b83180473eb0d3c010a1a7c6c4de)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

